{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And you shall love your fellow as yourself.</b> Love on behalf of your fellow what you would have loved on your own behalf had you reached his situation. And since the perfection of fear of El, blessed be He, is observance of the statutes — for one who observes them so as not to sin against Him can do so only because he has already recognized His greatness, that it is not fitting to rebel against His word, and has already recognized His goodness and knows that He commands only what is fitting and good even when the reason of the commandment is not disclosed — therefore He said:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:56.969689069Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}